# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Burmy — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT environment template.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never put a real secret in this file — it is committed.
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored and must stay so.
#
# Production (Netlify + Supabase) does not use this file at all — production
# environment variables live in Netlify's own dashboard, scoped and secret-
# marked per docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "Netlify environment-variable policy." This
# template covers local dev only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development, matching compose.dev.yml.
# In production the host is the internal `dbnet` service name, never localhost.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://burmy:burmy@localhost:5432/burmy

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development

# The ONE allowlisted identity. Checked against the verified Cloudflare Access
# JWT claim and again at session creation. There is no signup route.
OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com

# ── Authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Access with Google is the SOLE authentication mechanism. There is
# no in-app credential, no session cookie of Burmy's own, and no second factor
# — see docs/SECURITY.md, "Authentication".
#
# Verified against Cloudflare's JWKS in src/proxy.ts AND again inside
# requireOwner(), so a route the proxy matcher misses is still enforced.
#
# FAIL CLOSED: these are REQUIRED unless NODE_ENV is exactly `development`.
# Anything else — production, test, staging, or unset — with these missing makes
# the app refuse every request with 503 rather than serve traffic without the
# outer gate. A missing config is an outage; a skipped check is a breach.
#
# Left blank locally, where verification is bypassed by design (no Cloudflare).
# TEAM_DOMAIN accepts `burmy`, `burmy.cloudflareaccess.com`, or the full URL.
CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
CF_ACCESS_AUD=

# After Access is configured, provision the single owner row once:
#   pnpm db:provision-owner
# requireOwner() only ever RESOLVES this row by the verified email — it never
# creates one, so this step has to happen out of band, before the first sign-in.

# ── Game metadata (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Game metadata (cover art, genre, developer/publisher, critic score,
# playtime, ESRB rating) from IGDB (https://api-docs.igdb.com/), authenticated
# via Twitch's client-credentials OAuth flow. Register a free app at
# https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps (needs 2FA on the Twitch account) to get
# both values below.
# OPTIONAL — the Games module works fully without them, just without cover
# art or the fields that come with it. The test suite must pass with these
# unset.
IGDB_CLIENT_ID=
IGDB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Steam sync (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two separate consumers, both optional and both degrading gracefully without
# these set:
#   - The in-app sync (Library screen's "Sync with Steam" button, reviewed at
#     /games/sync/[runId] before anything is written) — see docs/GAMES.md,
#     "In-app Steam sync".
#   - scripts/sync-steam-library.mjs, a local-only CLI script with the
#     OPPOSITE fill-only-what's-null rule — see that script's header and
#     docs/GAMES.md, "Steam library sync" for its dry-run-by-default contract.
# Both read the exact same two vars below; there is only one Steam identity
# to configure.
#
# STEAM_API_KEY: a free Steam Web API key tied to the owner's account, from
# https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey (never expires, unlike IGDB's Twitch
# token).
# STEAM_ID: accepts EITHER the owner's 64-bit SteamID (SteamID64 — the
# 17-digit number, e.g. from a profile URL that already reads
# /profiles/<digits>, or from a lookup tool like https://steamid.io) OR a
# vanity name from a custom profile URL (steamcommunity.com/id/<name>, e.g.
# `burmyyy`) — a vanity name is resolved to a SteamID64 automatically via
# Steam's ResolveVanityURL endpoint before syncing, both in-app and in the
# script.
#
# OPTIONAL — like IGDB above, the app and its full test suite work fully with
# these unset. Without them, the in-app Sync button renders disabled with a
# visible explanation naming both vars (never hidden, never a crash), and
# scripts/sync-steam-library.mjs refuses to run at all. The owner's Steam
# profile "Game details" privacy must also be set to Public, or the API
# silently returns an empty games list with no error to tell the two
# situations apart.
STEAM_API_KEY=
STEAM_ID=
